193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (The Business Question: How can we accurately predict transaction profitability and identify the key drivers of profit and loss across different retail categories and regions?)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 135 0 R
/E (Key Finding & Recommended Action: The analysis revealed that while Furniture generates high revenue, it yields extremely low profit margins due to high discount rates, whereas Technology \(especially Copiers and Phones\) drives the majority of net profit. A Random Forest model successfully predicted profit with 92.79% accuracy based on sales and cost data. Action: We recommend revising the discount strategies in underperforming states \(like Texas and Ohio\) and reallocating marketing efforts toward high-margin Technology products.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
